// fmt
// #3691: an own-line comment breaks a trailing-comment alignment run, the
// same way a blank line or a code line with no trailing comment does
// (spec/FMT.md sec. 12) -- confirmed against gofmt's own tabwriter, which
// realigns the two sides of an interstitial own-line comment to two
// independent columns rather than spanning it. This pins that decision:
// the pgFirstWord/pgSecondWordLong pair below and the
// pgThirdWord/pgFourthWordVeryLong pair after the own-line note must land
// at DIFFERENT comment columns in .expected, proving the note is a hard
// break, not a no-op for alignment purposes.
fn pgFirstWord(): int { return 1 }       // first field
fn pgSecondWordLong(): int { return 22 } // second field
// An own-line provenance note interrupts the run here.
fn pgThirdWord(): int { return 333 }           // third field
fn pgFourthWordVeryLong(): int { return 4444 } // fourth field
